review reads that record\"): no citing TC states it (TC-178, TC-211, TC-399, nor the inspection procedure).\n- d. SR-161 C1/C2 in TC-211: neither TC-211 cell states them. They live only in the procedure the method delegates to. C2 is stated by TC-399's expected.\n\n**(3) TC clauses no LLR/SR sentence in the set states**\n- a. TC-399 expected \"verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated\", plus method \"non-ruling outcome line ... do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows\": no sentence in LLR-360 or SR-161 states that outcome lines leave verdict parsing unchanged.\n- b. TC-178 method COVERAGE: \"a tree whose rows carry no Hat-Refs at all exits zero under --strict and reports exactly one coverage advisory\" contradicts the code. th::test_a_spine_that_uses_the_cell_nowhere_gets_NO_advisories pins ZERO advisories for exactly that tree. The evidenced th::test_coverage_is_one_advisory_and_never_a_finding uses a tree with one filled cell, and it is unit-level, with no --strict run. LLR-183 states neither the gate-on-use behaviour nor \"exactly one\".\n- c. TC-399 method \"a non-round neither reads the roster\" has no LLR-360 sentence. LLR-360's \"an unreadable existing roster refuses composition\" reads unscoped, but pb::test_outside_a_round_the_roster_is_not_read and the slotless override show a malformed roster does NOT refuse outside a round or without a declared slot.\n- d. TC-178 method's roster-path equality pin: LLR-183 states only \"hats.py stays the sole validator\". The pin is arguably the test-side consequence.\n- e. (Not a real gap.) TC-211 expected's child-purpose and stopping clauses are stated by SR-186, which TC-211 verifies but which is outside this set.\n- f. TC-399 evidence ab::test_the_spine_authors_hats_value_puts_the_sittings_questions pins the coordinator author prompt (scripts/coordinator/mkprompt.py, terra-spine-prompt.template.md). No LLR-360 arm or TC-399 clause states it.\n\n**(4) Evidence nodes that do not exist**\n- All 30 named test nodes (TC-178 ×9, TC-399 ×21) and TC-211's evidence anchor exist.\n- TC-211 `inputs` names `docs/reviews/wi-976/011-ADJUDICATE-a46aad8.brief.md` and `docs/reviews/wi-976/011-ADJUDICATE-a46aad8.md`. Neither exists: the lane's reviews stop at 010, and a46aad8 is the telemetry commit \"session WI-976 verdict accepted\". This reads as a forward reference to the pending sitting. It must resolve once that sitting is filed, or the inspection inputs dangle.\n- TC-211's anchored result is a PASS from 2026-10-03, taken \"under the procedure as it then read\". The procedure has since changed, so the inspection is owed again.\n- Cosmetic: TC-399's evidence has no space after `;` between `...puts_the_sittings_questions` and `tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_an_override...`.\n\n**(5) LLR test_refs vs citing TCs**\n- None. LLR-183 test_refs \"(see TC-178)\" matches its only citing TC (TC-178). LLR-360 test_refs \"TC-399\" matches its only citing TC (TC-399, Drafted like LLR-360).\n\r\ntests/test_trace_hats.py ['test_the_design_tier_is_checked_too_and_names_its_own_id', 'test_an_absent_roster_file_reads_as_no_names', 'test_a_hat_no_row_is_attributable_to_is_reported']\r\ntests/test_adjudicate_brief.py ['test_the_spine_authors_hats_value_puts_the_sittings_questions']\r\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3721:[design.LLR-360]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3722-sr_refs = [\"SR-161\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3723-title = \"Perspective questions in a decomposition-round sitting\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3724-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/plan_briefs.py;project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/prompts/adjudicate-first-approval.template.md;project-trajectory/prompts/adjudicate-amendment.template.md\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3725-code_symbol = \"sitting_hat_block/round_hat_block/round_questions/fill_hat_slot/sitting_tail/hat_surface_for_work_item/NOT_A_ROUND/HAT_SLOT/HAT_PARENTS/_roster_refusal/compose/combined_values\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3726-detail = \"A sitting brief for a decomposition round carries every declared perspective question applicable to that round and asks the verdict to name one outcome for each perspective. A decomposition round judges a system requirement awaiting first approval or an approved stakeholder need whose text is amended; another judged set carries no perspective question. The applicable set combines each amended need with each need named by a system requirement the sitting judges, including an amended system requirement, widens each need by the authoring work item's declared tags, and evaluates each need alone. Questions fill the perspective slot only when the sitting template declares it; a template without that slot composes unchanged. A sitting composed from several judgement kinds carries the questions once. An absent roster yields its no-perspective line, while an unreadable existing roster refuses composition and names the roster.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3727-rationale = \"A decomposition review needs the applicable questions in the same brief and verdict that record its judgement. Treating each parent need independently prevents tags from one sibling widening another, while an optional slot preserves briefs that do not conduct a decomposition review.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3728-test_refs = \"TC-399\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3729-status = \"Drafted\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3730-component = \"CMP-008\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3731-phase = 5\n--\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml:1810:[test.TC-178]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1811-verifies = [\"SR-161\", \"LLR-183\"]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1812-level = \"Unit\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1813-method = \"\"\"Four halves, one per claim the row makes. RESOLUTION: build a spine whose SR and LLR rows carry a Hat-Refs naming a hat the roster declares and one naming a hat it does not, and assert the second is reported and joins the --strict failure set under its own class while the first is silent. VACUITY: delete the roster and assert the same tree reports nothing at all, then leave a roster that will not parse and assert the same - absence is opt-out for the layer, and a rule that reddened every row on a malformed roster would punish the wrong file. COVERAGE NEVER GATES: assert a tree whose rows carry no Hat-Refs at all exits zero under --strict and reports exactly one coverage advisory. THE DERIVED SET: assert effective_hats returns the union of a row's own refs with its SR parents', that a parent's change moves the child's answer with no child cell edited, and that a dangling SR-Refs contributes nothing rather than raising. Plus the anti-drift pin the second reader needs: assert trace's roster path equals hats.ROSTER_REL, since a test may import both modules where the shipped code may not.\"\"\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1814-tier = \"Full\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1815-expected = \"Satisfies LLR-183's Hat-Refs provenance, name-resolution, severity and effective-set mechanics; SR-161's perspective-review acceptance is inspected by TC-211.\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1816-automated = \"Yes\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1817-evidence = \"\"\"tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_an_undeclared_hat_name_is_a_finding; tests/test_trace_hats_driven.py::test_an_undeclared_hat_reds_a_real_run_under_strict; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_the_rule_is_vacuous_without_a_roster; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_an_unparseable_roster_is_vacuous_not_loud; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_coverage_is_one_advisory_and_never_a_finding; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_effective_hats_unions_the_parents; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_a_parent_re_ruling_moves_the_child_with_no_child_cell_edited; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_a_dangling_parent_contributes_nothing_rather_than_raising; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_the_roster_path_matches_the_hats_module\"\"\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1818-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1819-phase = 5\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1820-\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1821-[test.TC-180]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1822-verifies = [\"SR-139\", \"LLR-185\"]\n--\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml:3947:[test.TC-399]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3948-verifies = [\"SR-161\", \"LLR-360\"]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3949-level = \"Unit\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3950-method = \"Exercise each state of the hat block: a non-round neither reads the roster nor asks a perspective question; a first-approved system requirement or amended approved need makes the round, and every judged system requirement's need and every amended need is a parent; work-item tags widen one need without merging siblings; an absent roster supplies the no-perspective line; an unreadable roster refuses and names it; each applicable perspective receives one non-ruling outcome line; declared template slots receive the block while undeclared slots compose unchanged; a combined sitting carries one union block; and those outcome lines do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows.\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3951-tier = \"Full\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3952-expected = \"Satisfies LLR-360 (parent SR-161): a decomposition-round sitting presents each applicable perspective question and requires one outcome, while another sitting has no perspective question; optional-slot, combined-sitting, absent-roster, unreadable-roster, and verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated.\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3953-automated = \"Yes\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3954-evidence = \"tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_sitting_with_no_first_approval_sr_and_no_amended_need_says_it_is_no_decomposition_round; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_outside_a_round_the_roster_is_not_read; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_an_amended_need_is_a_parent_the_work_items_refs_do_not_reach; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_judged_sr_reaches_hats_through_the_need_it_names; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_the_work_items_tags_widen_each_need_and_sibling_needs_never_merge; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_an_absent_roster_yields_the_opt_out_line_in_a_round; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_malformed_roster_refuses_a_round_naming_the_roster; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_the_round_block_asks_one_outcome_line_per_hat_in_a_non_ruling_form; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_first_approval_of_a_drafted_sr_carries_the_hat_block; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_first_approval_of_llr_and_tc_rows_only_says_no_decomposition_round; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_an_amendment_of_an_approved_need_carries_the_hat_block; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_an_amendment_of_an_sr_only_says_no_decomposition_round; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_an_amendment_round_reaches_the_need_of_every_sr_it_judges; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_combined_round_reaches_the_need_of_an_sr_another_section_amends; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_the_spine_authors_hats_value_puts_the_sittings_questions;tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_an_override_without_the_hats_slot_composes_unchanged; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_combined_sitting_carries_the_hat_questions_once_over_the_union; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_combined_sitting_that_is_no_round_states_it_once; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_malformed_roster_refuses_a_round_sitting_by_name; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_no_other_brief_declares_the_hats_slot; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_hat_outcome_lines_change_no_ruling\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3955-status = \"Drafted\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-3956-phase = 5\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
